  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Ford Motor shows $619M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Ford Motor has 16,399 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $37.7K and obligations up 30.5% year over year. Ford Motor received uneven funding across recent years: FY21 obligations were $503M, FY22 obligations were $688M, FY23 obligations were $307M, FY24 obligations were $580M, FY25 obligations were $474M, and FY26 obligations are $619M. Ford Motor’s federal sales are concentrated in a single reported buying agency and a single NAICS market: the General Services Administration obligated $619M, and Automobile Manufacturing accounts for $619M of obligations. Ford Motor’s current-year totals are partial, covering fiscal year to date only. The data reflects contract obligations except where award-value totals are explicitly labeled as total contract values in other tables.",
